      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-17T00:24:31Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): generic LinuxCNC 3-axis mill post and machine\n\nA new built-in post \"LinuxCNC\" (assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps, .ngc) and a\ngeneric machine \"LinuxCNC 3-axis\", written from the public LinuxCNC 2.9\nG-code and M-code references, structured after our own tormach.cps with\nthe PathPilot assumptions removed.\n\n- Retract option: G53 G0 Z<safe_retract> from the machine file (refused\n  by name when unstated - never an assumed G53 G0 Z0, #435/#495), G91\n  G28/G30 Z0 (Z only), or none.\n- T<n> M6 then G43 H<n>; option to leave G43 (and the section G49) out\n  when the M6 remap applies the length.\n- G64 P<tolerance> or G61; M30 or M2; optional % delimiters; G91.1\n  stated; arcs and helices with incremental IJK.\n- G73/G81/G82/G83/G85/G86/G89 with G99; a floating-holder tap is G84;\n  a rigid tap is G33.1 Z K, only on a machine that states\n  rigid_tapping true (encoder), else refused by name.\n- Refused by name: control compensation, tilted moves, home after an\n  operation, non-positive tool numbers, G73/G83 with Q <= 0.\n\nThe machine mirror now also publishes rigidTappingStated (true only for\na stated rigid_tapping: true), since rigidTapping reads unstated as true.\n\nPinned by linuxcnc_post (9 tests), conformance (linuxcnc goldens),\nscript_linuxcnc, and the cross-post suites cycle_hop, ream_cycle, comp,\ncontrol_comp, wear_comp, post_spindle_rule_all, machine.\n\nFixes #2303\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
