      "message": "fix(post): LinuxCNC post writes G86 P0, posts G85 for a zero-dwell back-bore, refuses a G83 dwell\n\nCopies main's fixes on tormach.cps and grblhal.cps to the new\nlinuxcnc.cps (review of PR #2310, blockers 1-3):\n\n- Each opening G86 block writes a P word, P0 for no dwell. LinuxCNC\n  requires P on G86 (as #2362).\n- A back-bore with no dwell posts G85, not a G89 with no P (as #2360).\n- A positive G83 dwell is refused by name with the message text of\n  #2348. LinuxCNC G83 has no P word.\n\nPinned by adding linuxcnc to ZERO_DWELL_P0 and SECONDS\n(bore_cycle.rs), POSTS (dwell_cycles_modal_p.rs) and LINUXCNC_FAMILY\n(g83_dwell_linuxcnc.rs). Each list addition fails on the old script.\nNo golden changes.\n\nRefs #2303\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
